    "ensure": "Judge the parsed target declaration, using supplied helpers to establish its behavior. Do not flag an unrelated declaration merely present in context. Inspect loops or recursion that build a list or string. A growing accumulated prefix is not traversed or copied on every iteration by append, concatenate, or an equivalent visible helper. Such repeated prefix copying makes linear output construction quadratic. Prepending then reversing once, one final flatten, constant-time tree joins, and copying each disjoint chunk once are allowed. In Bend Base, List.append and String.append traverse their first argument. Appending a fixed-size first argument is allowed. Require a visible growing first argument and repetition; do not infer costs of unknown helpers or flag an isolated append. If absent, this rule holds.\n"
